Evaluate whether the assistant is stuck in a loop after the user's latest message.

A loop is repeated or substantially equivalent actions that are not making meaningful
progress toward the user's request. Examples include repeatedly invoking the same tool,
re-running the same failing command, rewriting the same instructions without changing
strategy, or cycling through the same state. Normal multi-step work, retries with a
materially different approach, and repeated status checks while work is progressing are
not loops.

